     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="ES">1) A total of 301 people were directly involved in training, counseling, interviews and workshops as part of our learning cycles. In the Domestic Work Cycle, 6 women participated in interviews, 27 domestic employees participated in exploration workshops, 101 people participated in a survey addressed to employers to explore the registration procedures of domestic work and social valuation (65 women - 36 men); and 151 people participate in IPS registration assessment (110 women and 40 men). In the apparel industry cycle, 6 people were interviewed during field visits (3 women and 3 man), Finally, 10 male and female operator employees participated in exploratory workshops (5 men - 5 women). Of the total number of people who participated directly in the learning cycles 216 were women.


2) A total of 15 key institutions and organizations accompanied activities related to the learning cycles linked to the National Formalization Strategy: 
 &#x2022; Goverment institutions: Instituto de Previsi&#xf3;n Social (IPS), Servicio Nacional de Promoci&#xf3;n Profesional (SNPP), Centro de Entrenamiento al Emprendedor (CEE), Direcci&#xf3;n de la Mujer Trabajadora (MTESS). 
 &#x2022; Local Government: Municipalidad de Yaguaron.
 &#x2022; Civil Society: Asociaci&#xf3;n de Confeccionistas y afines de Yaguaron, Sindicato de Trabajadoras del Servicio Dom&#xe9;stico de 
 Paraguay &#x2013; SINTRADESPY, Sindicato de Trabajadoras Dom&#xe9;sticas de Paraguay-Legitimo SINTRADO-L, Pro-Desarrollo, 
 Cooperativa Universitaria, Club Centenario y Club Internacional de Tenis (CIT).
 &#x2022; Private Sector: Fenix SA Cooperativa COOMECIPAR.
 &#x2022; Academy: Centro de Documentaci&#xf3;n (CDE). 


3) A total of 6 documents were published on the UNDP website and social networks. (www.py.undp.org), the Acceleration Labs Network (www.undp.org/acceleratorlabs) and the Ministry of Labor (www.mtess.gov.py):
